        "richtext_hT6Xga": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Fresh flowers cost $50 to $100 every week or two. You're spending $2,600 to $5,200 per year on something that dies. Think about what else you could do with $5,000. Actually, don't. It'll make you mad. One custom silk arrangement costs more upfront but lasts forever. Your kids will inherit it. Seriously.</p><p>Why artificial saves your money and mind:</p><ul><li>Pay once, never again</li><li>No more weekly \"should I buy flowers\" guilt</li><li>No emergency runs when you remember guests are coming</li><li>No throwing away something you just paid for</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
